Z||000000||kempo||08-20-2001||11:23 AM||||The Virginia police department has started issuing tickets...  "Intent to Speed"  Something to the effect of if you accelerate fast coming out of an intersection / red light / stop sign (whatever), and the cop sees you doing so, even though not going above the speed limit, can issue you a citation for "driving with the intent to speed."  What kind of bullsh*t is this?  Are there any other laws like this where you guys live?  ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Oreif||08-20-2001||11:40 AM||||"intent to speed"!?! :WTF:<P>Sounds like  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"><P>Here they can write one for squeeling tires but I've never heard of intent to speed. Hell, I'd get one a day if they did that here. Many times I'll wind up first gear on a major road. <BR>I bet you could fight it in court and win.<BR>That is like arresting people for walking into a store with no money in their pockets and holding an item for "intent to steal".<BR>To prove "intent" They would have to prove you "planned" to speed. Accelerating quickly does not mean your going to speed. If you "race" up to just under the speed limit and let off the gas their "intent to speed" is gone. If you race up to the speed limit then see the police car and hit your brakes then I could see the "intent" part. ||||reg||13
Z||000002||fierohoho||08-20-2001||12:08 PM||||kempo, get a copy of the ordinance or statute from them and post it so we can go over it, there must be some wording in there that justifies that type of offense, sounds pretty weak to me though.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
