Z||000009||ChadMan||08-20-2001||01:05 PM||||Accelerating fast is "intent to speed"?  That's as stupid as claiming that buying a lighter is "intent to commit arson."<P>I hate to sound like rayb, but that sounds like a gold-plated excuse to screw with young guys (age profiling?).  No way in hell is a 45-year-old white guy with a Boxster going to get that ticket.||||reg||8
Z||000010||MinnGreenGT||08-20-2001||01:10 PM||||Here in Minn I've heard of people getting tickets for "excessive acceleration" when launching from a light or squealing the tires (or lighting them up!)  I've never been nailed on it (only for speeding) but I think I'd put up a fight- especially on the VA ticket that is a load of  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig2.jpg">    <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||08-20-2001||01:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>Here in Minn I've heard of people getting tickets for "excessive acceleration" when launching from a light or squealing the tires (or lighting them up!)  I've never been nailed on it (only for speeding) but I think I'd put up a fight- especially on the VA ticket that is a load of   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, in NC, if you spin your tires, they can get you for Careless & Reckless driving, because you are driving your car in a manner that causes it to loose traction, and therefore, loosing some control.  It's a pretty nasty ticket, 4 points, I believe.  <P>As for "Intent to Speed,"  well, they can suck my exhaust fumes on that one.  If I don't vere out of my lane, don't break traction, don't exceed the speed limit and signal as necessary - they can kiss my A$$!  And I would SO fight that in court.  But since I'm thirtysometing instead of a teenage, I'm not likely to get one.  Especially since I don't go to VA all that often, either.  Still, I'd love to see the actual statute.<BR>||||reg||13
