Z||000021||Haagster||08-20-2001||05:42 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>CA's had EOS for hundreds of years. The cop has to prove nothing more than the fact that they wrote the ticket.<P>You pay.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What you're saying is if a cop is pissed off at the world, or just doesn't like what you are driving, you pay?!?  Sorry, but there isn't a ticket written that cannot be challenged in court, especially one that charges "intent".  Doesn't mean you'll win...<p>[This message has been edited by Haagster (edited 08-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||kempo||08-20-2001||08:29 PM||||Indeed this is a pile of BS.  A friend of mine with a Lightning got this ticket for accelerating quickly from a light.  I'll try to get an ordinience of it and post it.  Next time I am at a red light with a cop, you're darn sure I'll be accelerating to the posted speed limit as quickly as my fiero will go, and if I get pulled, something to the effect of, "I also intended to get home from your wifes house before you get off from work."  See how he likes that as an excuse for "intending to speed."<P>-Kemp||||reg||3
